[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"670","stub":{"id":"670","section":"1319 to  Hwy 44 (5.37 miles)","altname":"","river":"Plum Creek","difficulty":"IIstandoutIII","states":["USA-KEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The property owner at the put in asks that paddlers take the gravel drive down the shore line and park at the last barn on the right. Pull into the fenced area outside the barn and park along the fence. DRIVE SLOW ON THE PROPERTY. The property owner has many dogs, and kids. Plus wet ground causes ruts. Obey her rules or donÂt park on her property. On a side note: The stone house is on the National Register of Historic Places.","id":"2424","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Putin","distance":"0","photoID":"13797","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"As soon as you put in, you will see some waves popping up on the river left side, shortly after that, you'll come to the 1st ledge. Run this ledge about 15 feet off the river left side to miss the worst of the hole. You can skirt it completely by hugging the left shore. Photo is the first playwave above the ledge.","id":"429","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"1st Ledge","distance":"0.1","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"13800"},{"type":"rapid","description":"When the swinging bridge is in sight, be ready for \"The Slide\". At 2.0 feet, it feels like sliding down a sliding board, at 2.5 and higher, it feels like you're on a really fast conveyor belt.\nDon't worry, though, there's no hole at the bottom... Left Side is usually deeper.","id":"430","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"The Slide","distance":"1.9","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"playspot","description":"A series over 10+ Surf waves back to back.","id":"2422","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Surf City","distance":"2","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"hazard","description":"Another series of surf waves. Be sure to check the bridge below for wood before you surf.","id":"2425","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"First Bridge Waves","distance":"2.83","photoID":"13799","difficulty":"II","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"A rapid with a hole on far river left, and far river right. River left flows into several trees and a large tree over hangs river right. Best move is middle left to middle right.","id":"2443","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Sycamore","distance":"3.4","photoID":"13812","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"Little Plum Creek adds more water to the creek after the 2nd bridge. A strong hole on the left after the bridge starts another nice series of play waves.","id":"2417","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Little Plum Hole","distance":"3.64","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"13801"},{"type":"playspot","description":"The best wave/hole at medium to high water. Wide, with a huge foam pile. No eddy access but you can walk back up on river right shore. Those not wanting to surf run on far river right or left.","id":"2411","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Feather Bed","distance":"3.9","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"13798"},{"type":"hazard","description":"\"Buddy's Hole\" lies in wait (waiting to put the munch on you) under the 4th car bridge. Eddy out on river right above it and run either right of the bridge support at higher water or left of it the rest of the time and skirt the hole.\nIf you're feeling froggy, jump in the hole, although, it may keep you for awhile. A great play wave with eddy service is just below.","id":"431","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Buddy's Hole","distance":"4.1","photoID":"7268","difficulty":"III","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"Best Play spot with eddy service on the river. Great Park and Play spot if you don't have a shuttle.","id":"2426","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Lower Buddy's Play Spot","distance":"4.11","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"7480"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Waterford Park is the takeout on river left before the Hwy 44 bridge. Enjoy the Swingset.","id":"2412","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Take out Playground","distance":"5.37","photoID":"13803","difficulty":null,"approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"13800","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"First Surf Wave","poi_name":"First Surf Wave","subject":"Todd","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"2425","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13800","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13800"}},{"id":"13803","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Takeout","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13803","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13803"}},{"id":"13812","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Bottom of Sycamore","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13812","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13812"}},{"id":"13797","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Plum Putin Parking","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13797","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13797"}},{"id":"13798","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Great Surfing Wave","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13798","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13798"}},{"id":"9118","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Plum Creek Access Map","poi_name":"","subject":"How to get there!","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9118","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9118"}},{"id":"7268","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6940","description":"","caption":"Upper Hole Buddy's","poi_name":"","subject":"Kyle Nicholson","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7268","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7268"}},{"id":"7481","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6941","description":"","caption":"Ben Surfing","poi_name":"","subject":"Ben ","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7481","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7481"}},{"id":"8171","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6942","description":"","caption":"High Water Plum Wave","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8171","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8171"}},{"id":"13801","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"Start of the Lower Plum","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13801","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13801"}},{"id":"7269","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"","caption":"Lower Buddy's","poi_name":"Buddy's Hole","subject":"","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"431","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7269","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7269"}},{"id":"7478","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6941","description":"","caption":" Surfing Below Buddy's","poi_name":"Surf Spot Below Buddy's","subject":"Richard Millea","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"2426","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7478","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7478"}},{"id":"7479","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6941","description":"","caption":"Buddy's from the top Eddy","poi_name":"Buddy's","subject":"Brian Sandmann","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"431","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7479","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7479"}},{"id":"7480","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6941","description":"","caption":"The Jim Gunn Show","poi_name":"Buddy's","subject":"Jim Gunn","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"431","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7480","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7480"}},{"id":"13799","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6939","description":"Check for wood before you surf.","caption":"First Bridge Waves","poi_name":"First Bridge Waves","subject":"","author":"Kyle Nicholson","poi_id":"2425","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13799","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13799"}}],"detail":{"id":"670","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Plum Creek is the best play run for Louisville area boaters. 5 miles with over 50 playspots. Point your bow up stream and catch a wave, if you miss one another will quickly follow. Flowing along the Bullitt and Spencer county line the creek runs only a few days a year. Look for thunderstorms bringing 1.5\"+ of rain to the area. Before the rain stops head to the river as the water will not last long.\n\nAs far as hazards, it's a narrow stream that is pretty much a flush from top to bottom, with very few eddies, strainers are a possibility. There are 3 bridges on the run and each of these should be approached with caution since the pilings can trap logs pretty easily. Class II-III skills are adequate if you are comfortable reading water on the fly.","averageGradient":"22","maxGradient":"30","length":"5.4","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["2424","429","430","2422","2425","2443","2417","2411","431","2426","2412"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-85.43493758263588,38.10207813890771],[-85.4349179778282,38.102069807524686],[-85.43460277782873,38.10200660752474],[-85.43438457782906,38.10169780752523],[-85.43399777782963,38.101702874191915],[-85.43357077783033,38.10145047419229],[-85.43301697783119,38.10079207419329],[-85.43287991116472,38.100457074193855],[-85.43271637783164,38.10041787419391],[-85.43284557783142,38.10022767419417],[-85.4329211778313,38.09952700752859],[-85.43285011116478,38.099377207528846],[-85.43290611116471,38.09931020752896],[-85.43276897783159,38.09897520752946],[-85.43269331116501,38.098214474197334],[-85.43225137783236,38.097422207531906],[-85.43226677783235,38.09731580753203],[-85.43212457783255,38.09701620753253],[-85.43206877783263,38.09676000753291],[-85.43212017783259,38.09608220753399],[-85.43271597783166,38.09484100753588],[-85.43333177783069,38.09410427420369],[-85.43365737783017,38.093773407537526],[-85.43440511116233,38.09340720753812],[-85.4347053111619,38.09325360753838],[-85.43479677782841,38.09326147420501],[-85.43584971116013,38.09270627420585],[-85.4365515778257,38.09233607420646],[-85.43798097782349,38.0914184075412],[-85.43800151115